WEBVTT

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:23.950
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:31.290
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:39.060
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:45.160
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.870
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:57.650
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:04.620
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:12.550
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:20.230
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.380
"One Way"

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.920
FILE. 41
ROUND IT GOES!
THE FIERY PATROL
LIGHT (PART 1)

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.300
You don't seem to be injured, but to be
safe, you'd better go to the hospital.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.340
We'll take you right there.
Just keep still.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.250
An unmarked black
Z patrol car?

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:18.480
That's right. He
tried to kill me.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.750
Was he alone?

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.830
There were two patrol bikes. Detective,
this is Bokuto's jurisdiction, right?

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:33.630
Does Bokuto have hit men working
for them?! They almost killed me!

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.260
How are you going to
make this up to me?!

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.340
Hey, punk...

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.540
Do you really have the guts to
pick a fight with a cop?

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:51.210
Well, do you?

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.260
What is this?! Are the cops hiring
Yakuza now, or something?

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.460
This is ridiculous!

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.410
Man, it's hot.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.070
The incident occurred last night
at two in the morning.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.540
Superb driving
skills.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.610
They achieved their goal without
killing their victim.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.050
Their goal, sir?

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.810
Terror.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.750
They wanted to scare their
victim half to death.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.490
It was clearly a carefully
planned operation.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:36.860
The teamwork between the unmarked car
and the bikes was excellent.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.160
It's as if they were
real cops.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.400
Idiot.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.280
They must be wannabes.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.710
Based on?

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.680
It was just an idea.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:54.680
The investigation team will
be looking into that.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.880
Man, it'll be tough pounding the
pavement, in this heat.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:04.860
As for us... We'll keep in close
touch with the investigators...

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.690
...and keep a lookout for that black
Z and the two patrol bikes.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.390
We'll use a special
code for this case.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.370
The code number
is 009.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.700
I'm going out.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.670
I'm going out.
009?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:22.270
Yes. Nine. We've got a problem
and only have one life left.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.980
Think they'll show up again?

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.110
Think they'll show up again?
We can't be sure, but I have a feeling.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.090
Impersonating police officers,
and causing accidents...

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.490
...means that they're doing
it for thrills.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:43.530
So I don't think it's just
a one-shot thing.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.710
<i>"There've been too many problems</i>
<i>at Bokuto Station!"</i>

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:42.450
<i>"But you've never had anything</i>
<i>this big before."</i>

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.950
<i>"The suggestion</i>
<i>that..."</i>

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.130
<i>"...this crime involves Bokuto Station..."</i>

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.250
"Enough. The public thinks it's true."

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.330
<i>"We've got to clear this</i>
<i>up immediately."</i>

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.600
<i>"Put everyone on the investigation,</i>
<i>even the Traffic Section."</i>

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.640
<i>"Do whatever it takes!"</i>

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:09.580
009 sighted near the Maruki Bridge in
Kinshigawa, Suehiro District.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.710
The driver is slightly injured. Units near
Central Hospital, please respond.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.480
The black Z was last
seen heading east.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.550
Requesting emergency
back-up.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.990
Same as last time. A black
Z and two patrol bikes.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.890
Merciless impostors!

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.550
Detective Tokuno.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.820
I don't think they're just
cop wannabes.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.230
Which means we have to
rethink the situation.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.810
You think so
too, huh?

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.910
I don't think wannabes
would go this far.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.070
Explain.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.510
They'd have to have serious guts to
pick a fight with us cops.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.850
I don't think mere wanna-
bes would be up to it.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.820
I see.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:58.180
All these faxes
are protests.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.580
"I condemn the Traffic Bureau
of Bokuto Station."

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:09.420
"I refuse to cooperate with
the police anymore."

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:14.230
"This is so disconcerting, that I feel I
cannot let my children play outside."

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.030
"I am thoroughly disappointed
with the police."

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:21.770
"I've never liked the motorbike
cops at Bokuto Station."

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.210
What?!

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:26.110
What?!
I don't know which will happen first...

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.940
...either the fax will burn out, or the station
will be flooded with protesters.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.410
What is it?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:37.580
People have been staring at
us when we're on patrol...

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.990
So that's what's
going on.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:43.330
The public is certain that the
black Z is one of our units.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.130
They would.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.170
The public aren't the only
ones with suspicions.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.290
Inspector Arizuka.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:24.600
We've got no leads, not even a plate number,
for the car involved in the two chases.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.600
That's all
we have.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:35.310
All right. A task force will be head-
quartered here at Bokuto Station.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.820
This is a strong request from
Police Headquarters...

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.040
...the Administrative
Chief, and myself.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:47.220
This is a serious problem which affects
not only Bokuto Station...

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.920
...but the entire
police force.

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:55.130
Starting tomorrow, except for emergencies,
there will be no patrols for one week.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.170
That includes patrol cars
and motorbikes.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.210
But sir, what's the point of...

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.440
But sir, what's the point of...
That's an order!

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:06.340
You have no choice
in this matter.

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.650
You cannot ignore
public opinion.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.690
The impostors keep
showing up...

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.720
...in a car with a patrol light and
on the two police bikes.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.320
They deliberately cause
the accidents.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.400
The public's trust in the police
has bottomed out.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:24.660
"Traffic Section"

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.030
And with regard to the identities
of these culprits...

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:33.540
...Headquarters has not
ruled out police staff.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.800
Based on the findings of
our investigation...

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:39.440
...the Public Security Commission
may have to take action.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.550
You don't have
much time.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:50.350
I want these impostors appre-
hended within the week.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.090
Officers with spare time will go
and get a change of clothes.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:57.560
That is all.
Move out.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:12.710
"Musashi knows Sake."

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.840
This is ridiculous.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:44.570
What're they thinking, anyway? Do they really
think our motorbike cops are involved?

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:50.580
Take it easy, Natsumi. They've
just raised the possibility.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:54.050
If it's just a possibility, how
come Arizuka's here?

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.680
Anyway, the important thing
is to catch them quickly.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.830
Catch them.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.570
What if it's
one of us?

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:32.990
"009 Task Force"

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:37.020
The two incidents have nothing
in common.

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:39.690
If there is a third incident, we may
be able to establish a pattern.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.200
Of course, we'd like to prevent
a third incident.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.610
Of course.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.630
Perhaps they'll show up tonight.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.180
I could just curl up and fall
asleep when I get home.

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:04.190
You can't! We're just going
to pick up some clothes.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:25.370
There's a big U-turn
up ahead.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.510
Nikaidou here.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.970
Yoriko! Over here!

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.920
Reporting a 009 entering the Suehiro
Shopping District. Repeat.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:37.210
Reporting a 009 entering the Suehiro
Shopping District.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.670
Have you found
out something?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.460
Detective.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.340
The 009 has surfaced! Nikaidou and
Aoi are in pursuit!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.920
Here they
come.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.260
No, Yoriko!

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.360
It's like a
ghost.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.180
What's the car that just left?

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.780
What's the car that just left?
A patrol car...

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:47.220
Why did Tsujimoto and Kobayakawa
disobey my orders? Explain!

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.190
Why?!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.800
Because...

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:56.270
I believe it's because of their
pride, as police officers.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:01.140
Is pride going to help them
apprehend the culprits?

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:07.980
Officers cannot become exceptional
at their work without pride, sir.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:17.010
Please... please
stop.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:19.850
Just what do you guys think
you're trying to pull?!

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.000
Yoriko! Get off
the road!

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:45.950
Yoriko!

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.350
Are you out
of your mind?!

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.960
I was so upset I lost control.
It was so scary!

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.430
You all right?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.400
Nakajima.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.540
How'd you find out?

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.370
The station called me.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.110
Thank you.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:10.070
Those who are framed must hang together.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:15.340
The 009 is passing through Section 2 of
Suehiro District into Kaneuchi District.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:20.090
According to eyewitness reports, there
is one motorcycle and one car.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:23.350
The bike is a V Max. Nakajima
is in pursuit.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:26.420
Nakajima's on
his own bike.

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:30.550
He's got a strong sense of justice.
I hope he doesn't get in trouble.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:36.330
Kill the radios! Do it now! The
009 could be listening in!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:37.670
"009 Task Force"

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.200
Do you realize what
you're saying?!

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:41.340
Yes!

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:46.550
My officers are doing all they can...

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:49.780
Spare me your half-baked sentiments.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.080
What is it?

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:03.700
Inspector, I have something important to
tell you and the Section Chief in private.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.430
We're all cops here.
Go ahead.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:12.000
I see. Well, if that's the
way you feel, I'll say it.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:17.740
But if word of this leaks out, we can
kiss our pensions good-bye.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:19.470
Don't be
stupid.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:21.510
I'm serious.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:26.280
This could blow
up in your face.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:37.490
Attention all units. All radio com-
munications are to cease.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.430
Units are advised to act
on their own discretion.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:44.460
Meaning someone's tapping
into the police channel?

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.470
No, that's impossible.

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:50.030
Our scrambled digital radios aren't
available to the public.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:57.550
So that means that it's
got to be an insider.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.490
You won't
get away.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:13.290
Kobayakawa! What
are you doing?

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:20.970
Tell me.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.370
Inspector.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:27.810
Go ahead. Not much can shock
me, coming from Bokuto.

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:33.920
All right. The 009 are probably
real police officers.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:39.510
One of the victims says he heard police
radio chatter coming from inside the Z.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.220
They've been listening in
on our communications.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.560
What?!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:47.430
So that's why we've
gone silent.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.660
And another
thing...

00:20:50.470 --> 00:21:00.780
We got a tip that they're using
the frequency of 316.02 MHz.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:09.090
316.02 MHz. Used only
by Headquarters.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.430
Oh my God!

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.960
What?! You're trying
to hit me?!

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:39.940
Nakajima!

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:42.020
My leg! Ow,
my leg!

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.390
I'll call an ambulance!

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:50.590
I'll call an ambulance!
Nakajima! Nakajima!

00:21:55.700 --> 00:22:01.910
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:11.820
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:18.710
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:28.840
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:42.810
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:51.020
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:59.670
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:07.700
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.810 --> 00:23:17.270
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:24.760
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.120
"Long term painful effort"

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:31.060
What!? Nakajima's vanished
from the hospital?!

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.360
Oh, no!

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.430
Sorry, Miyuki! Let me
do this my way.

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:42.640
Inspector Arizuka, we desperately need
200 patrol cars for this mission!

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:46.710
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 42...

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:49.050
..."'Round it goes! The Fiery
Patrol Light (Part 2)."

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:52.120
I'm gonna make you
pay for this!
